From 51cbb41081da63b046e1ed49819619548d002c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mokhtar Yasser <mokhtar200301@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:58:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ads from the first game: no three free games any more

---
 privacy/index.html | 2 +-
 terms/index.html   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/privacy/index.html b/privacy/index.html
index 08639e7..b229052 100644
--- a/privacy/index.html
+++ b/privacy/index.html
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
       <p>To run outrepd: matches, rankings, Adventure, friends, notifications, your profile, keeping the game fair, and answering you when you contact us. And to show ads to accounts without Pro, as described under <a href="#ads">Ads</a>. Apart from those ads, we do not use your data for advertising, we do not build profiles of you for anyone else, and we do not use analytics tools. Crash reports are used only to fix the app.</p>
 
       <h2 id="ads">Ads</h2>
-      <p>outrepd is free to use and shows an ad when you leave the result of a game. There are no ads in your first three games, and none at all with OUTREPD Pro. The ads come from Google AdMob and are limited to content rated for teens.</p>
+      <p>outrepd is free to use and shows an ad when you leave the result of a game. There are none at all with OUTREPD Pro. The ads come from Google AdMob and are limited to content rated for teens.</p>
       <p>To choose, show and measure ads and to prevent ad fraud, Google receives information from your phone: your IP address, device and app information, how you interact with the ad, and your phone's advertising identifier where it is available. Google's policies cover what it does with it: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>
       <p><strong>On iPhone,</strong> the app asks before your advertising identifier can be used to track you (Apple's App Tracking Transparency). If you say no, it is not shared, and the ads are not personalised with it. You can change your answer in Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Tracking.</p>
       <p><strong>On Android,</strong> you can reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's settings (Settings → Google → Ads, or Settings → Privacy → Ads).</p>
diff --git a/terms/index.html b/terms/index.html
index b4c57e4..6539b16 100644
--- a/terms/index.html
+++ b/terms/index.html
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
       <p>outrepd is free to use and shows ads (see 6a). We may change, add or remove features, reset the ladder, or stop offering outrepd. We do not promise the app will always be available or free of errors, or that any rank or result will be kept.</p>
 
       <h2>6a. Ads and OUTREPD Pro</h2>
-      <p>outrepd shows an ad when you leave the result of a game, after your first three games. What is collected for the ads is explained in the <a href="/privacy#ads">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
+      <p>outrepd shows an ad when you leave the result of a game, unless you have OUTREPD Pro. What is collected for the ads is explained in the <a href="/privacy#ads">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
       <p>OUTREPD Pro is an optional subscription, weekly or yearly, that removes the ads. Every mode can be played without it. The price and period are shown before you buy, in your currency, and you pay through Google Play or the App Store under their terms.</p>
       <p><strong>It renews automatically</strong> at the end of each period, for the same length and at the then-current price, until you cancel. Your store account is charged within 24 hours before each renewal.</p>
       <p><strong>You can cancel at any time</strong> in Google Play → Payments &amp; subscriptions, or on iPhone in Settings → your name → Subscriptions. You keep Pro until the end of the period you have paid for. Deleting your outrepd account or the app does not cancel a subscription.</p>
-- 
